 {} [:a {:href "/venues/2173"} "Grand Palais Éphémère, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2007304"} "22 from 22 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Israeli " [:a {:href "/athletes/143940"} "Inbar Lanir"] " came to Paris 2024 as the world’s top ranked judoka in the class. She was the 2023 World Champion, had won the 2023 World Masters, and had won a bronze medal in the mixed team event at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics. " [:a {:href "/athletes/144399"} "Shori Hamada"] " was the defending gold medalist but was only the third-ranked Japanese judoka in the class, and Japan would put forward " [:a {:href "/athletes/153291"} "Rika Takayama"] " to represent them."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143306"} "Anna-Maria Wagner"] " (GER) had won the recent 2024 World Championships at 78 kg and was a World Champion in 2021. She had won a bronze medal in the class at Tokyo 2020, losing the final to Hamada. Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144057"} "Alice Bellandi"] " competed at Tokyo 2020 in the 70 kg class but had moved up to 78 kg since then. She was runner-up to Wagner at the 2024 World Championships and also won a bronze medal at the Worlds in 2023. She was world ranked #3 as of June 2024."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This class went mostly according to chalk, as the favorites advanced, with the exception of France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/142747"} "Madeleine Malonga"] ", who won gold in the team event and was a silver medalist at Tokyo, but lost in her first match against Portugal’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146017"} "Patrícia Sampaio"] ". The final came down to Bellandi against Lanir but there was not a lot of action, with Bellandi winning by " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " using " [:em {} "sode-tsurikomi-goshi"] ", although it was ultimately decided when Lanir received her third " [:em {} "shido"] " at 3:26."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Takayama lost her quarter-final match against Wagner, and both would advance to the bronze medal matches, but neither would win. Takayama lost to Sampaio by " [:em {} "ippon"] " after two " [:em {} "waza aris"] ", while China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141708"} "Ma Zhenzhao"] " defeated Wagner by " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " in extra time."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144057"} "Alice Bellandi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143940"} "Inbar Lanir"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ISR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ISR.png"}] "ISR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141708"} "Ma Zhenzhao"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146017"} "Patrícia Sampaio"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POR.png"}] "POR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143306"} "Anna-Maria Wagner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "G